[thin] Numerical threshold boundary at the complete nominal 3 mm setting-tool sections. All seven emitted pairs recover 3.000 mm in the actual native export: fore/aft fork cheeks, tip-stop plate and base. The source-defined fixture is identical to that export, and dock-lint-review.json binds every pair and STL/STEP hash. This tool holds a bare machined stem before BPT fitting; printed setting accuracy remains unqualified.
alternatives: Adding stock solely to move an exact 3 mm cheek, stop or base past numerical ranking changes the bench tool without correcting a smaller nominal section. Use an explicit numerical tolerance at that boundary and measure the actual tip-to-flange register before factory use.
